Phase 2 (FullSpectrum engine emission, P2A): explicitly propagate
ExtrusionEntity::inset_idx through ExtrusionMultiPath and ExtrusionLoop
copy / move constructors and assignment operators.

Why: inset_idx is a base-class member of ExtrusionEntity (added by
OrcaSlicer upstream for inner/outer/inner perimeter ordering). When
ExtrusionMultiPath / ExtrusionLoop define their own copy constructors,
the base class falls back to default-construction unless explicitly
chained — so inset_idx silently resets to -1 on every copy / assign /
container reallocation. That breaks the FullSpectrum Pointillisme
router (which uses inset_idx to decide which physical extruder a given
perimeter index gets routed to) and the existing Orca inner/outer
classic perimeter ordering pass.

Mechanical port from FS v0.9.9 commit b3c41fda
(`ratdoux/OrcaSlicer-FullSpectrum@v0.9.9`), no behavior change for
prints that don't use mixed filaments — they were already getting
inset_idx propagated via the upstream classic perimeter path that
sets it before any cross-derived-class assignment.

Companion to patches 0030 (PerimeterGenerator.cpp populates
inset_idx on emitted Loops / MultiPaths) and 0031 (VariableWidth gap
fill quality fix).

